此外，你还可以在那里重温誓言。

1141
00:44:55.810 --> 00:44:56.290
Okay.
好吧。

1142
00:44:56.770 --> 00:44:57.310
All right.
行吧。

1143
00:44:57.650 --> 00:44:59.710
Toby suggests that Jim go to Amsterdam.
托比建议吉姆去阿姆斯特丹。

1144
00:45:00.010 --> 00:45:04.330
He says he went there after his divorce for a week or maybe a month.
他说他在离婚后去过那儿一个星期，或者也许有一个月。

1145
00:45:04.450 --> 00:45:05.250
He can't remember.
他记不清了。

1146
00:45:05.830 --> 00:45:08.190
Creed says he should go to Hong Kong.
克里德说他应该去香港。

1147
00:45:08.350 --> 00:45:12.610
Creed also calls John Jimmy, and I feel like you can see John about to break.
克里德还叫约翰“吉米”，我觉得你能看出约翰快要笑场了。

1148
00:45:12.610 --> 00:45:13.490
He's like, Jimmy!
他就像是在喊：吉米！

1149
00:45:14.410 --> 00:45:17.950
And I swear John has this, like, he's kind of got this side smile.
我发誓约翰当时有这种，怎么说呢，他脸上带著那种标志性的侧笑。

1150
00:45:18.630 --> 00:45:22.310
Well, at 9 minutes, 29 seconds, Creed has a talking head.
好吧，在 9 分 29 秒的时候，克里德有一个单独访谈镜头。

1151
00:45:22.610 --> 00:45:26.530
For anyone wondering, Creed is speaking Mandarin.
如果有谁在好奇，克里德刚才说的是普通话。

1152
00:45:26.850 --> 00:45:27.210
Yeah.
对。

1153
00:45:27.450 --> 00:45:29.790
And he says, hello, my Chinese friends.
他说的是，你好，我的中国朋友们。

1154
00:45:30.270 --> 00:45:31.910
That's what he's saying in Mandarin.
他用普通话说的就是这个。

1155
00:45:32.170 --> 00:45:33.410
I reached out to Creed.
我联系了克里德。

1156
00:45:33.530 --> 00:45:33.770
Yeah?
是吗？

1157
00:45:33.770 --> 00:45:36.850
Because we had a fan question from KKPL Watson.
因为我们收到了一个来自KKPL Watson的粉丝提问。

1158
00:45:37.370 --> 00:45:41.890
He said, at various times, Creed has spoken Japanese and Chinese on the show.
他说，克里德在剧中有好几次都说过日语和中文。

1159
00:45:42.010 --> 00:45:43.330
Does he really speak either?
他真的会这两种语言吗？

1160
00:45:44.330 --> 00:45:46.030
So, I texted Creed.
于是，我给克里德发了短信。

1161
00:45:46.310 --> 00:45:47.330
Oh, I can't wait.
哦，我等不及了。

1162
00:45:47.390 --> 00:45:48.170
What was his response?
他的回复是什么？

1163
00:45:48.450 --> 00:45:49.370
Here's what he said.
他是这么说的。

1164
00:45:49.510 --> 00:45:50.430
Did he say, who are you?
他是不是说，你是谁？

1165
00:45:50.550 --> 00:45:50.850
No.
没有。

1166
00:45:51.310 --> 00:45:52.770
But again, I wasn't sure.
不过话说回来，我也不确定。

1167
00:45:53.170 --> 00:46:02.290
He said, when I was in Germany in 1964, I conversed in a rudimentary fashion because I'd studied a year in college.
他说，1964我在德国的时候，由于在大学学过一年，还能进行初级的交流。

1168
00:46:02.850 --> 00:46:04.850
But he said he hasn't used it since.
但他说他之后就再没用过了。

1169
00:46:05.370 --> 00:46:15.710
He says he does not speak Japanese or Mandarin or Cantonese, which is actually the language they speak in Hong Kong, mostly, not Mandarin.
他说他不会日语、普通话或粤语，香港那边主要说的是粤语，其实并不是普通话。

1170
00:46:15.910 --> 00:46:21.750
But he said, I do have a made-up language that I've been trying to get accepted.
不过他说，我确实有一种自己编的语言，我一直想让大家接受。

1171
00:46:21.950 --> 00:46:22.750
That I believe.
这个我信。

1172
00:46:22.930 --> 00:46:28.130
But he's been meeting resistance, and he used it during his stint as manager for that week at Dunder Mifflin.
但他一直遭到抵制，而且他在邓德米夫林当了一周经理的那段期间就用过这门语言。

1173
00:46:28.470 --> 00:46:29.470
Oh, my God.
我的天哪。

1174
00:46:29.690 --> 00:46:30.770
This is Creed, guys.
这就是克里德，伙计们。

1175
00:46:30.790 --> 00:46:31.170
That's Creed.
那就是克里德。

1176
00:46:31.170 --> 00:46:31.830
This is Creed.
这就是克里德。

1177
00:46:37.220 --> 00:46:37.800
All right.
好吧。

1178
00:46:37.900 --> 00:46:41.680
At 9 minutes, 57 seconds, my character smiles.
在9分57秒的时候，我的角色笑了。

1179
00:46:42.400 --> 00:46:44.440
This doesn't happen very often.
这种情况可不常见。

1180
00:46:44.660 --> 00:46:49.280
And Jenna, I did one of our little dorky actor-y things where I gave myself a backstory.
而且珍娜，我当时做了一件我们演员那种有点书呆子气的举动，我给自己设计了一个背景故事。

1181
00:46:49.780 --> 00:46:51.080
For this little smile?
就为了这个小小的微笑？

1182
00:46:51.220 --> 00:46:52.060
For this little moment.
就为了这短短的一刻。

1183
00:46:52.380 --> 00:46:53.940
So, it wasn't scripted.
所以，这不是剧本里写好的。

1184
00:46:54.140 --> 00:46:58.220
But in the conference room, Dwight is going to now do his speech for us.
但在会议室里，德怀特接下来要给我们发表他的演讲。

1185
00:46:58.420 --> 00:46:59.800
He has his note cards, right?
他拿着他的手卡，对吧？

1186
00:47:01.020 --> 00:47:07.140
And I just sort of gave myself this backstory that he had probably practiced this in front of me, that we had worked on it together.
我只是给自己设计了一个背景故事，觉得他可能在我面前练习过这个，我们一起排练过。

1187
00:47:07.640 --> 00:47:13.560
And so, I just really beam as he gets up there, and I look around to make sure, is everyone watching?
所以，当他站上去的时候，我整个人都在发光，而且我环顾四周确认大家是不是都在看？

1188
00:47:13.860 --> 00:47:15.240
Because I'm really proud of him.
因为我真的为他感到骄傲。

1189
00:47:15.340 --> 00:47:15.560
Yeah.
对。

1190
00:47:15.560 --> 00:47:17.140
So, I just had this little thing.
所以，我当时就有这么个小细节。

1191
00:47:17.140 --> 00:47:17.820
I gave myself.
我给自己加的。

1192
00:47:18.020 --> 00:47:18.740
I didn't tell anyone.
我没告诉任何人。

1193
00:47:18.980 --> 00:47:25.700
But Randall and Matt, our camera operators, they caught it, and it made it in.
但是我们的摄像师兰德尔和马特捕捉到了，而且剪进正片里了。

1194
00:47:25.840 --> 00:47:26.140
Oh.
哦。

1195
00:47:26.220 --> 00:47:27.540
And they would often do that.
他们经常那样做。

1196
00:47:27.660 --> 00:47:33.120
Randall and Matt would sort of catch these little moments that we did in the background that weren't part of the script.
兰德尔和马特会捕捉到我们在背景里做的那些不属于剧本的小瞬间。

1197
00:47:33.120 --> 00:47:39.640
And they were so great about sort of finding those moments and making sure that everyone saw them.
他们非常擅长捕捉这些瞬间，并确保每个人都能看到。

1198
00:47:39.800 --> 00:47:42.280
I just like that all of us all the time,
我只是喜欢我们所有人在任何时候，

1199
00:47:42.280 --> 00:47:53.880
we were so invested in our characters and how our character would react to a moment or to a story that even if we hadn't been directed or didn't think the camera was on us,
都对自己的角色以及角色会对某一刻或某个故事做出什么反应投入了极大的热情，以至于哪怕我们没有被导演要求，或者觉得镜头没有对着我们，

1200
00:47:54.000 --> 00:47:57.520
we would stay in our characters and react in the moment.
我们也会留在角色状态里，当场做出反应。

1201
00:47:57.720 --> 00:47:57.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1202
00:47:58.280 --> 00:48:00.660
And that's an example of one of those that made it in.
这就是那种成功入选的例子。

1203
00:48:00.660 --> 00:48:00.960
Yeah.
没错。

1204
00:48:01.120 --> 00:48:03.780
And I remember Matt saying, Ange, I see what you're doing.
我记得马特说过，安吉，我懂你在做什么。

1205
00:48:04.020 --> 00:48:05.060
I'm going to clock it.
我要把它记下来。

1206
00:48:05.180 --> 00:48:05.720
I caught it.
我抓到了。

1207
00:48:05.920 --> 00:48:08.460
That was always so fun when they would notice our little choices.
每当他们注意到我们的小心思时，总是那么有趣。

1208
00:48:08.720 --> 00:48:08.960
Yeah.
对。

1209
00:48:09.380 --> 00:48:09.760
Aw.
噢。

1210
00:48:09.980 --> 00:48:10.820
I love that.
我太喜欢这样了。

1211
00:48:10.940 --> 00:48:11.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1212
00:48:11.960 --> 00:48:19.780
Well, then we go to Jim and Dwight's desks, Angela, and Dwight is talking all about he's going to go to New Zealand.
好了，然后我们来到吉姆和德怀特的办公桌前，安吉拉，德怀特喋喋不休地说他要去新西兰。

1213
00:48:20.640 --> 00:48:21.220
I don't know.
我不知道。

